        "id": 1724998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-30T23:01:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see.. So, `snapshotctl map-snapshots` is what you are looking for; however, that wouldn\u0027t do the merge post reboot. It will allow mounting partitions over the snapshot.",
      "parentUuid": "a1e4bd91_b6d573a0",
      "revId": "1b435d929bf416a90fe06106ff1603b1b0cb4a29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e944bca_6d369595",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4554676
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-30T23:18:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for review, map-snapshots likely won\u0027t be sufficient as we\u0027re flashing for CI where both we need to wipe userdata and also there may be later reboots which would otherwise revert the mounted snapshots.\n\nSo apply-snapshots still looks like the correct command, as I want the device flashed but with performance/flash-wear improvement of using apply-update instead of a full fastboot flash.\n\nHowever, I have no guarantee that the b slot will have a working bootloader (or any bootloader) prior to the HAL switch slot. This means using `apply-update` and rebooting to bootloader results in the device failing to boot to bootloader.\n\nFrom your `apply-update.sh`, this is the step that fails in that case: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/core/fs_mgr/libsnapshot/scripts/apply-update.sh;l\u003d230-232",
      "parentUuid": "e3ae151b_77d0d684",
      "revId": "1b435d929bf416a90fe06106ff1603b1b0cb4a29",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a3da0a5_0aef6a95",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1724998
